runtime changes: 0.4.37 → 0.4.38
## 0.4.38

- Security questions lead default `check` and `audit`; result-exposure advice groups by table and creation advice ignores defaults and literal-only assignments. New questions cover evidence, money, approval bypasses, stale eligibility, inconsistent windows, role-wide writes, private create/edit asymmetry and evidence removal.
- Existing apps can now fail `check` on retained role grants or optional uploads that contradict explicit non-null or parent integrity intent. Repair the finding or acknowledge each ID with `check --ack-security <ID> --reason "<decision>"`. The source-bound decision lives in `snapback/security-reviews.json`; bulk `--ack-notes` does not clear it, and source/analyzer changes require renewed review. Deliberate optionality remains quiet; fresh starters pass without stock upload acknowledgments.
- `test` explores directed lifecycle histories beyond pairs. The security guide explains review decisions; rule recipes model ownership of a particular wall. These bounded histories and naming-based questions do not certify application security.
- Seeded staging accounts carry their session kind. Existing partial online session literals use bearer-only transport; complete and local/device sessions retain strict validation. `E_SESSION` names every invalid/missing field and shows the token-only repair.
- `advance()` reports again coerce to numeric `now` for arithmetic and `Date`. Staging jumps preserve live session lifetimes by default; `{sessions:"expire"}` tests expiry. `{drain:false}` pauses maintenance for mutation deadline tests and `drain()` resumes at the same time. Held future boundaries refuse before effects unless `allowHeld` is explicit; already-processed current windows remain not-due. Production clock controls remain refused.
- Staging clock publication follows credential persistence. Captured write/effect outcomes retain close-cutoff custody; stale authentication refusals cannot fail writes after bearer rotation or successor sign-out.
- Upgrade warnings apply to actual version transitions and affected scripts, include partial-session/numeric-advance scans, and record piped delivery. Fresh init is quiet. Old quiet CLIs can hide captured migration advice. Future store formats name a newer Snapback and `sql` exits nonzero.
- React and Expo starter lists use `ReadState`. Password clients omit witness/persona plumbing; proof drivers install the observer. Proof text matching accepts composed React Native text and wrapping labels while retaining strict ambiguity and explicit matching modes.
History begins at 0.4.26; earlier changes are not recorded.
